10	- For every effective degree-six divisor Gamma, H^0(C,omega_C tensor W_5^vee(Gamma)) is nonzero exactly when O_C(Gamma) is isomorphic to W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}. [evidence: mechanical; The obstruction line bundle has degree zero, and a degree-zero line bundle on a smooth projective connected curve has a nonzero section exactly when it is trivial.]
11	- On a balanced tetragonal genus-six cover with fibre divisor D, W_5 is isomorphic to omega_C^{tensor 2}(-D), so W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1} is isomorphic to omega_C(-D). [evidence: mechanical; Relative duality gives O_{P(E^vee)}(1)|_C = omega_C tensor gamma^*O(2); squaring and tensoring by gamma^*O(-5), with gamma^*O(1)=O_C(D), yields the identities.]
12	- The degree-six failure condition on the balanced tetragonal locus is Gamma in |omega_C(-D)|, equivalently D+Gamma is canonical. [evidence: mechanical; Combine O_C(Gamma)=W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1} with W_5 tensor omega_C^{-1}=omega_C(-D).]
13	- The reduced-support locus in a relative degree-six linear system is open, and ordering six distinct support points gives a finite etale S_6-cover. [evidence: mechanical; Reducedness and pairwise distinctness form the complement of the relative discriminant; the free permutation action on six ordered distinct points has quotient the unordered reduced divisor.]
