24	- A finite etale cover of an open subset of M_{0,n} has pure Tate cohomology because the base has pure Tate cohomology. [reason: Finite etale pushforward introduces nontrivial local systems. Monodromy, including braid-group monodromy, can produce non-Tate mixed Hodge structures even when the base has Tate cohomology.]
25	- Passing to a finite etale S_6-cover changes rational cohomology only by additional Tate summands because all rational S_6-representations are defined over Q. [reason: The field of definition of the deck-group representations does not determine their Hodge type; cohomology with the associated monodromic local systems can be non-Tate.]
26	- The closed evaluation-failure locus may be replaced by its balanced reduced-support top stratum in localization. [reason: Unbalanced splitting types, non-reduced divisors, and jumping-linear-system strata remain in the closed locus and may contribute to Borel-Moore homology and boundary maps.]
27	- A singular stratified closed locus of top codimension four yields the displayed ordinary-cohomology Gysin sequence H^{18}(Z)(-4) to H^{26}(M). [reason: That purity-form Gysin map requires suitable smoothness or a regular pure-codimension embedding. For a singular, non-pure stratified locus one must use cohomology with supports or Borel-Moore homology and account separately for all strata.]
28	- Positive-codimension strata cannot contribute to the weight-26 degree-26 term solely because they have smaller dimension. [reason: Dimension alone does not eliminate their appropriately shifted cohomology or the connecting and residue maps in a stratification spectral sequence.]
