- The evaluation-failure locus Z associated to O_C(Γ)≅W_5⊗ω_C^{-1} is nonempty for (g,n)=(6,6).
- Every residual pair on the RED-0001 list with ordinary degree equal to vcd and genus at least two—(3,12),(5,8),(6,6),(7,4),(8,2)—is killed by top-degree rational vanishing of the pure mapping class group.

## Mathematical constraints

- Cite Church–Farb–Putman as proving H^{4g-4+n}(Mod_{g,n};Q)=0 for every n>=1 (with Mod_{g,n} the pure/ordered mapping class group), and conclude H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)=0. [reason: The published theorem covers Mod_g, Mod_{g,*}, and Mod_{g,1} only; it supplies no top-vcd vanishing for PMod_{6,6} at degree 4g-4+n=26, so the transport to H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q) is unsupported.]
- From the claimed vanishing H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)=0, conclude W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)=0 and hence that the exact group is the empty direct sum of Q(8). [reason: The weight-piece and empty-sum conclusions are valid implications from whole-group vanishing, but the premise H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)=0 is not established by the cited input, so the conclusions do not follow.]
- Treat arbitrary-puncture at-vcd vanishing as already available from the residual degree/vcd bookkeeping alone. [reason: Equality of ordinary degree with vcd only shows that vanishing strictly above vcd is inert; it does not prove vanishing exactly at vcd for PMod_{g,n}.]

## Reusable computations

- None recorded.

## Dependencies to resolve

- A correct theorem establishing H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)=0, or equivalently top-degree rational vanishing H^{4g-4+n}(PMod_{g,n};Q)=0 at (g,n)=(6,6).
- If ambient vanishing is unavailable: identification of components, dimensions, stabilizers, and finite-cover behaviour of the evaluation-failure locus Z, and a proof that the exact codimension-13 contribution supported on Z is of Tate type Q(8) (or an exhibited surviving non-Tate summand).
- Independent discharge of the geometric sub-dependencies: h^0-stratification of the relative degree-six linear system |W_5⊗ω_C^{-1}|, comparison of determinantal/Fitting ideals with the Abel–Jacobi incidence scheme, and control of Gysin/localisation and monodromy on strata of Z.
