    {"id": "C66-GEO-Z-C7", "statement": "The determinantal presentation of Z has expected codimension 6 while codim Z = 4; Z carries excess dimension 2 and is nowhere cut out by a regular sequence in that presentation. A codimension-4 Gysin map is legitimate only over the Petri-general open where Z is smooth.", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["C66-GEO-Z-C1", "C66-GEO-Z-C6"]},
    {"id": "C66-GEO-Z-C8", "statement": "Z -> [Z/S_6] is a finite etale S_6-torsor of algebraic stacks with [Z/S_6] the reduced-support open of the relative degree-six effective-divisor incidence stack; the analogous coarse-space statement is false because curve automorphisms give nontrivial stabilizers.", "status": "proved", "depends_on": ["finite-group-quotient-stack-torsor"]},
